'' Two things that only fail together. '.i' inside WITH did not parse, and the
'' resulting FBX0400 made 'if 0 = len( .i ) then' followed by 'end if' look like a
'' SINGLE-LINE if rather than a block if with an empty body -- so the 'end if' was
'' consumed by the wrong construct, and a namespace closed early. The compensating
'' bug hid the real one: fixing the IF alone made the symbol names worse, not better.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ast tests/parser/src/with-member.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: FBX0400
